    {
      "id": "fbcyabm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO ENVIRONMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The environment consists of biotic (living) and abiotic (non-living) components working together.",
        "Natural resources are divided into renewable (inexhaustible) and non-renewable (exhaustible) categories.",
        "Deforestation causes severe ecological impacts, including global warming, biodiversity loss, floods, and droughts.",
        "Soil erosion is defined as the removal of the top fertile layer of soil.",
        "Global warming is driven by greenhouse gases produced through fossil fuel burning, deforestation, and industrial activities."
      ],
      "id": "y52kiu0"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Environment Components",
          "value": "2 Types (Biotic & Abiotic)",
